title: The Hamburg Uprising
subtitle: In Hamburg, the rising begins anyway.
new-page: true
tags: rf_event
view-if: year = 1923 and chemnitz_seen = 1 and chemnitz_strike = 0
max-visits: 1

= The Hamburg Uprising

On the morning of 23 October, armed Communists in Hamburg storm police stations in Barmbek, Schiffbek and other districts. The rest of Germany stays quiet. Whether the courier calling off the rising failed to arrive in time, or the Hamburg leaders chose to go ahead, is still argued over by historians.

[? if player == "left" or player == "stalin" : Hamburg is your ground. Word can still reach the fighters. ?]

- @let_fight: Let Hamburg fight. Someone must show that the party meant it.
- @stop: Send word to break off and save the cadres.
- @watch: The rising is in the leadership's hands.

@let_fight
view-if: player == "left" or player == "stalin"
on-arrival: {!
Q.repression += 15;
Q.members -= 12;
Q.readiness -= 5;
Q[Q.player + '_strength'] += 5;
Q[Q.player + '_moscow'] += 4;
Q.spd_relation -= 5;
!}

For three days a few hundred fighters hold out against the police and naval units. Dozens are killed on both sides. The party will make it a legend. [? if player == "stalin" : Thälmann's name will be tied to it for the rest of his life, though his actual part in it is unclear. ?]

@stop
view-if: player == "left" or player == "stalin"
on-arrival: {!
Q.repression += 6;
Q.members -= 4;
Q[Q.player + '_strength'] -= 2;
Q.readiness += 2;
!}

The fighters withdraw on the second day and hide their weapons. Fewer die. Some of your own people call it a betrayal.

@watch
view-if: player != "left" and player != "stalin"
on-arrival: {!
Q.repression += 15;
Q.members -= 10;
Q.readiness -= 5;
Q.left_strength += 3;
Q.spd_relation -= 5;
!}

For three days a few hundred fighters hold out against the police and naval units. Dozens are killed on both sides. The Left will use Hamburg against the leadership that left it alone.
